            <div xml:id="d734">

                <pb facs="0709" n="701" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg701"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/10761: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Leahy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vichy</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-09T12:00:00+02:00">May 9, 1941—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        May 9—9:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>526. We were told in confidence by a Government official yesterday that
                    instructions have been sent to the High Commissioner in Syria that in the event
                    German planes fly over Syria toward Iraq they should not be fired upon; that if
                    any of them should land in Syria they should not be permitted to depart pending
                    instructions to be requested <pb facs="0710" n="702" xml:id="pg702"/> from
                    Vichy. If on the other hand British planes should fly over Syria the High
                    Commissioner’s instructions are to endeavor to shoot them down.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Beirut.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leahy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
